AI Automation and Digital Literacy Cohort 2: Full Curriculum
Vixora Academy · 12 weeks · Draft v1 for review
Course Overview
This beginner-friendly course teaches students to use AI tools and no-code automation to work faster and earn more. Students start with digital literacy, learn to prompt AI tools well, then build real automations and AI assistants for everyday and business tasks. The course ends with a portfolio project and a clear path to offering automation services.
* Duration: 12 weeks
* Format: Online / Physical (hybrid)
* Level: Beginner (no coding required)
* Pricing: ₦30,000
* Certificate: Awarded on completion, with a portfolio project
Learning Outcomes
By the end of the course, students will be able to:
* Use computers, cloud tools and the internet safely and confidently
* Write clear prompts that get useful results from AI tools
* Use AI to speed up writing, research, planning and spreadsheet work
* Design and build no-code automations that connect everyday apps
* Build a simple AI assistant or chatbot
* Automate common business tasks such as email, lead follow-up and social media
* Package and price automation work for clients or employers
Tools Used
ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini (AI assistants), Excel or Google Sheets, Google Workspace, Zapier and Make (no-code automation), and a no-code chatbot builder. Alternatives such as n8n can be added if preferred.
Course Structure
* Phase 1: Foundations (Weeks 1-3): digital literacy, AI basics, prompting
* Phase 2: AI for Productivity (Weeks 4-5): writing, research, planning, Excel with AI
* Phase 3: Automation (Weeks 6-9): workflows, no-code builds, agents and chatbots, business automations
* Phase 4: Application and Career (Weeks 10-12): portfolio project and monetizing skills
Assessment (Proposed)
* Weekly practical assignments
* Mid-course practical (prompting and one working automation)
* Portfolio project: a working automation or AI assistant with documentation and a short demo
* Certificate issued on completing all weekly deliverables and the portfolio project
Week 1: Digital Literacy Foundations
Objectives
* Build confidence with devices, files and online tools
* Learn the safe-use basics
Topics
* Files, folders and cloud storage (Google Drive)
* Email, calendars and online collaboration
* Search skills and judging online information
* Passwords, two-factor authentication and common scams
* Setting up the accounts needed for the course
Hands-on
* Organize a cloud folder system
* Set up all course accounts securely
Deliverable: organized workspace and account checklist
Week 2: Introduction to AI and the Main AI Tools
Objectives
* Understand what AI is and what it can and cannot do
* Get comfortable with the main AI assistants
Topics
* What AI, machine learning and large language models are, in plain language
* What AI does well and where it fails (mistakes, made-up facts, bias)
* Tour of ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini
* Responsible use: privacy, honesty and checking outputs
Hands-on
* Try the same tasks in three AI tools and compare the results
Deliverable: AI tools comparison sheet
Week 3: Prompt Engineering
Objectives
* Write prompts that produce reliable, useful results
* Build a personal prompt library
Topics
* The parts of a good prompt: role, context, task, format, constraints
* Giving examples and step-by-step instructions
* Improving a weak prompt through iteration
* Reusable prompt templates
* Common prompting mistakes
Hands-on
* Rewrite ten weak prompts into strong ones
* Build prompt templates for your own work
Deliverable: personal prompt library (at least 10 templates)
Week 4: AI for Writing, Research and Planning
Objectives
* Use AI to save time on everyday knowledge work
* Check AI output before using it
Topics
* Drafting and editing emails, documents and reports
* Summarizing long documents and meetings
* Research with AI and verifying sources
* Planning: schedules, project plans and to-do systems
* AI note-taking and transcription tools
Hands-on
* Produce a research summary and a work plan using AI, with fact-checking
Deliverable: research summary and plan, with a short fact-check note
Week 5: Excel and AI for Work
Objectives
* Use spreadsheets effectively with AI help
* Clean and analyze simple data faster
Topics
* Spreadsheet basics: formulas, sorting, filtering, charts
* Using AI to write and explain formulas
* Cleaning and organizing data with AI help
* Summarizing data and spotting trends
* Checking AI-generated formulas for errors
Hands-on
* Build a small business tracker with AI-assisted formulas
Deliverable: working spreadsheet tracker
Week 6: Workflow Automation Basics
Objectives
* Think in workflows
* Plan an automation before building it
Topics
* What automation is and where it pays off
* Triggers, actions and conditions
* Mapping a manual process into steps
* Choosing tasks worth automating
* How apps connect: APIs and webhooks, in plain language
Hands-on
* Map three of your own repetitive tasks as workflow diagrams
Deliverable: workflow maps with one chosen to build
Week 7: Building Automations with No-Code Tools
Objectives
* Build working automations in Zapier and Make
* Test and fix automations
Topics
* Zapier: triggers, actions, filters and multi-step workflows
* Make: scenarios, modules and routers
* Connecting Gmail, Google Sheets, Calendar and forms
* Testing, error handling and monitoring
* Free plan limits and costs
Hands-on
* Build a form-to-spreadsheet-to-email automation
* Build the same flow in both tools and compare
Deliverable: two working automations with screenshots
Week 8: AI Agents and Chatbots
Objectives
* Understand how AI assistants and agents work
* Build a simple chatbot for a real use case
Topics
* Chatbots versus agents: the difference
* Giving an AI instructions and knowledge (custom assistants)
* Building a no-code chatbot for FAQs or customer support
* Adding AI steps inside automations
* Limits, safety and when a human should step in
Hands-on
* Build and test a chatbot for a small business scenario
Deliverable: working chatbot with a test log
Week 9: Automating Business Tasks
Objectives
* Apply automation to common business workflows
* Combine AI and automation in one flow
Topics
* Email: sorting, auto-replies and AI-drafted responses
